      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "title": "Overview",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Charlie 'Bird' Parker (1920–1955) revolutionised alto saxophone with bebop — fast harmonic rhythm, chromatic lines, improvisation on chord changes."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "compositions",
      "title": "Compositions",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "*Confirmation*, *Blues for Alice*, *Ko-Ko*, *Ornithology* (based on *How High the Moon*). Tunes became études for jazz musicians worldwide."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "practice-ethic",
      "title": "Practice ethic",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Legendary woodshedding — 11–15 hours daily in youth. Oral tradition plus rigorous technique produces new vocabulary."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "for-trad-improvisers",
      "title": "For trad improvisers",
      "level": 2,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "Target chord tones on strong beats; chromatic approaches between. Apply sparingly on modal tunes."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
